            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "About 50 minutes",
            "text": "<p>About 40 minutes start to finish. The rice cooks and the sauce blends while the fish sits drying, so the hands-on stretch is short and the air fryer is only six to eight minutes of it.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_serves": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "users",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Serves 4",
            "text": "<p>Serves 4. Four 6 oz Steelhead portions &mdash; two 2-Packs &mdash; over about three cups of cooked jasmine rice. Halves cleanly, and the tzatziki keeps two days either way.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_prep": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Watch for the C",
            "text": "<p>Pat the cubes dry, then leave them uncovered in the fridge while you make the sauce. A dry surface is what browns; a wet one steams.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
