      "settings": {
        "section_id": "building-the-sauce",
        "liquid": "<style>\n  .sea-sheet {\n    --ink: #171717;\n    --muted: #5c5c5c;\n    --line: #e5e2dc;\n    --wash: #faf8f4;\n    --gold: #bb8f50;\n    color: var(--ink);\n    background: var(--wash);\n    border: 1px solid var(--line);\n    border-radius: 20px;\n    padding: 30px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__eyebrow {\n    font-size: 11px;\n    letter-spacing: .14em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    color: var(--gold);\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin: 0 0 8px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__heading {\n    font-size: clamp(23px, 2.8vw, 30px);\n    line-height: 1.15;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin: 0 0 10px;\n    max-width: 22ch;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__lede {\n    font-size: 15px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    margin: 0 0 24px;\n    max-width: 68ch;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__cols {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));\n    gap: 14px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col {\n    background: #fff;\n    border: 1px solid var(--line);\n    border-radius: 14px;\n    padding: 18px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col--pick {\n    border-color: var(--gold);\n    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--gold);\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__num {\n    display: inline-flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    width: 26px;\n    height: 26px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    background: var(--ink);\n    color: #fff;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin: 0 0 10px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col h3 {\n    font-size: 15.5px;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n    margin: 0 0 7px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col p {\n    font-size: 13.5px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__foot {\n    margin: 18px 0 0;\n    padding-top: 14px;\n    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);\n    font-size: 13px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n  @media (max-width: 749px) {\n    .sea-sheet {\n      padding: 22px;\n    }\n    .sea-sheet__cols {\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n    }\n  }\n\n  .sea-sheet__fig {\n    margin: 22px auto 0;\n    max-width: 360px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__fig img {\n    width: 100%;\n    height: auto;\n    display: block;\n    border-radius: 16px;\n    box-shadow: 0 14px 34px -22px rgba(0,0,0,.5);\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__figcap {\n    margin: 10px auto 0;\n    max-width: 360px;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"sea-sheet\">\n  <p class=\"sea-sheet__eyebrow\">How the sauce actually gets built</p>\n  <h2 class=\"sea-sheet__heading\">The avocado is the thickener &mdash; which is why the cucumber has to go in dry.</h2>\n  <p class=\"sea-sheet__lede\">\n    A classic tzatziki is strained yogurt and not much else. This one carries a whole avocado, and\n    that is what gives it the colour and enough body to sit on top of hot fish instead of running\n    off it. Three moves, and the order matters for exactly one reason: water.\n  </p>\n\n  <div class=\"sea-sheet__cols\">\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col sea-sheet__col--pick\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">1</span>\n      <h3>Squeeze the cucumber dry</h3>\n      <p>Grate half a cup and wring it out in a clean towel until no more comes. Cucumber is mostly\n      water and it will keep releasing into the sauce for an hour after blending &mdash; that is how\n      a thick tzatziki turns into a thin one in the fridge.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">2</span>\n      <h3>Everything in at once</h3>\n      <p>Yogurt, avocado, the squeezed cucumber, dill, parsley, mint, garlic, lemon juice, olive oil,\n      salt and pepper. No need to build it in stages &mdash; there is nothing hot in the jug, so it\n      goes straight to smooth and bright green.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">3</span>\n      <h3>Loosen last, a spoon at a time</h3>\n      <p>Cold water, one tablespoon at a time, until it pours in a ribbon rather than a blob. Adding\n      it at the start means you cannot tell how thick the avocado made it, and a sauce you have\n      over-thinned cannot be taken back.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <figure class=\"sea-sheet__fig\">\n    <img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0222/9882/0682/files/2_7f607006-11a5-42e2-9209-787a945b8b92.png?width=760\" alt=\"Green goddess tzatziki pouring from the blender into a dish\" width=\"939\" height=\"1675\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n    <figcaption class=\"sea-sheet__figcap\">\n      Pourable, not runny. It should fall in a ribbon and hold its shape for a second on the surface.\n    </figcaption>\n  </figure>\n</div>",
